course: dictionary
lesson: 1532
title: Certain: sure, particular, or some
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Certain has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. Ask yourself: is someone sure about something, or is the word pointing at one particular thing or some things?
explain: «I am certain» means I am sure, with no doubt at all. «Are you certain?» asks whether someone is sure. Phrases like «for certain» and «make certain» are about being sure too.
explain: «A certain boy in our class» does not mean the boy is sure of anything. Here certain means one particular boy, and the writer does not name him. «Certain foods» means some foods. The word after certain is the clue: if it is a, or a word for more than one thing, certain is not about being sure.
fact: Certain means sure, with no doubt.
fact: A certain thing is one that will happen for sure.
fact: «A certain» means one particular person or thing that is not named: «a certain boy in our class».
fact: Before a plural word, certain means some: «certain foods».
fact: In maths chance, certain is the top of the scale: impossible, unlikely, even chance, likely, certain. A certain event always happens.
exercise: «I am certain the answer is seven.» What does certain mean here? | Missing | Some answers | *Sure, with no doubt | A particular answer that is not named
exercise: «The school zone sign means cars must drive slower at certain times.» What does certain mean in this sentence? | Sure, with no doubt | *Some particular times | Certain to be late | Very early
exercise: In maths chance, which word means an event always happens? | Likely | Even chance | *Certain | Unlikely
test: «Speed is how far something goes in a certain time.» What does certain mean here? | Very slow | *A particular time that is not named | Sure, for certain | Some times
test: «Are you certain?» What does certain mean in this question? | Not sure at all | *Asking whether you are sure | A plural word for some | Hidden
exam: Which sentence uses certain to mean some? | A certain boy waved to me. | *Certain children like to swim. | I am certain I locked the door.
